      "static_counterexample_or_fault_trace": "Ring records store birth task/table. SHARE changes that task current table without migrating or retaining an authorized historical ring-custody action. TASK_EXIT marks task dead without refusing surviving ring references. _ring then requires an alive task currently owning the old table; C ring slot/end impose the same live/current table match. Retirement after either transition is refused, while TABLE_END/OFD_END continue to reject the surviving ring/alias. This is a Source state-machine counterexample, not a captured kernel order.",
